  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Owen, you're verified. I can see the order: you were charged for 2 beef pho at $15 each, and it was handed over today at 6:41 PM, so it's within the reporting window. The restaurant didn't mark anything unavailable, so nothing has been refunded yet for the missing pho.\n\nYou have two options for the missing pho:\n\n1. **Refund to your Visa ending 4242:** $12.00. That's the $15.00 price minus its $3.00 share of your WELCOME10 promo discount. The $3.00 promo share is added to your account as credit.\n2. **Account credit only:** $18.00. That's the $15.00 price plus 20%, for use on a future order.\n\nWhich would you prefer?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks for checking. I'd rather have the money back on my Visa, so option 1 works for me. Before I agree, though, I'm not sure I follow the $3 promo part. I used a welcome code, but I don't remember how much it was for. Can you tell me what it was and how the $3 share got worked out?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Your WELCOME10 code took $10.00 off the order. Here's how the $3.00 share is worked out:\n\n- The discount applies across the whole order, whose subtotal was $50.00 (2 pho at $15 each, spring rolls at $7, banh mi at $13).\n- The missing pho is $15.00 of that $50.00, which is 30% of the order.\n- Its share of the discount is 30% of $10.00, so $3.00.\n\nYou never paid that $3.00 for the missing pho, because the promo covered it. So the card refund is $15.00 \u2212 $3.00 = **$12.00**. The $3.00 promo share comes back to you as account credit.\n\nIn total you'd get $12.00 on your Visa ending 4242 and $3.00 in account credit. Do you want me to go ahead?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Yes, go ahead with the $12 back on my Visa and the $3 credit. Thanks for sorting it out."
  }
